## Design Craft Guidance

Formwork's design-craft floor — the visitor-mode taxonomy (Persuade / Operate /
Read / Experience), the anti-pattern rule set and its thresholds, the
color-strategy vocabulary (Restrained / Committed / Full palette / Drenched),
and the `.formwork/design-system.md` section structure — is **derived design
guidance**, adapted from prior art in AI-generated-UI anti-pattern detection:

**Impeccable** — https://impeccable.style — https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable
Copyright 2025 Paul Bakaus. Licensed under the
[Apache License 2.0](https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable/blob/main/LICENSE).

Impeccable in turn credits Anthropic's
[frontend-design](https://github.com/anthropics/skills/tree/main/skills/frontend-design)
skill as its starting point.

### What is and is not shared

No Impeccable code ships in Formwork. `formwork design-lint` is an
independent Rust implementation: its own CDP client, its own WCAG contrast
math, its own rule evaluation, and its own static fallback engine. What carries
over is the *design judgment* — which patterns are worth flagging and at what
threshold — expressed in our own rule vocabulary and severity model.

Impeccable's detector engine, browser adapters, command surface, scoring
rubrics, and configuration formats are not used.

